#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096445 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096648 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "27d5c96d-ca13-5c1e-83d3-0dc9f6da0f83" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Vectors are Parallel"}] :question/id #uuid "069b2882-f4a9-589f-a903-4e89d077cd85" :question/math-academy-id "e-4279" :question/problem "Suppose, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$. Given that $7\\mathbf{a}+14\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\lambda \\left(3\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b} \\right)$ are equal vectors, find the scalar factor $\\lambda$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\n7\\mathbf{a}+14\\mathbf{b}= \\dfrac{7}{3} (3\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=\\dfrac{7}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096446 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc49f831-8e1d-5fb4-8952-1dd4ee3bfa02" :knowledge-point/title "Creating Parallel Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "d1329498-4413-5d87-a814-be0d57a3afd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4280" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf a$ is shown in the diagram below. Draw the vectors $2\\mathbf a$ and $-3\\mathbf a$.\n\n![](images/a5/a5eaa8baaf303ecbfa6c0fb207d6b19836cc90fc331e238cd473109f44fddf80.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $2\\mathbf{a}$ and $-3\\mathbf{a}$ must be parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nNow, for the vector $2\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $2\\mathbf{a}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $2\\mathbf{a}$ have the same direction since the factor $2$ is positive.\n\n![](images/41/41eba7e6c5bbe420418726bd45efa668dc6be5ff5144ba35d52b53a43925c333.png)\n\nNext, for the vector $-3\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $3\\mathbf{a}$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $-3\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions since the factor $-3$ is negative.\n\n![](images/ed/eda3f2572d98ef1789292ec6d35569487b32efa459673dcb95f8fdd0d1f4ae5b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096494 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc5bab6c-1ce7-58b5-a59d-cff2ce35ecca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "11c09a26-0e83-5a77-b777-aea8a3594960" :question/math-academy-id "e-5183" :question/problem "Consider the diagram that is shown below. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\mathbf{b}=-\\mathbf{c}$\n2. $\\mathbf{e}=2\\mathbf{a}$\n3. $\\mathbf{a}=2\\mathbf{e}$\n\n![](images/95/95ae711c1ccbf7543e6d269aa8d817a66e2ac348113ea71f3a1babcbb23d1ca3.png)" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ have different magnitudes. So, $\\mathbf{b} \\neq -\\mathbf{c}$.\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{e}$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{e}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Statement III is false. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$ is greater than the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq 2\\mathbf{e}$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc49f831-8e1d-5fb4-8952-1dd4ee3bfa02" :knowledge-point/title "Creating Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8ce19e-7310-5653-bd81-7663f10f1275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/505d9eb880fb166f11d45858b34a2aa3491a6772da6266e1954c383ebc97a905.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571560} {:answer/id #uuid "10d35a2d-dc1a-5fbd-93b5-a142a14eec4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fd554195222a46ab5fcefdb3ca601fdcba5a0daeba16ce3faae2bc6c9371bb3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571567} {:answer/id #uuid "34d29957-a4c2-51f3-8772-9c52f4ca375c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c3/c371c84dedc8f76fe286a7f4201416c2c344d4718bdf61a80bd5c3da7a048cd4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571626} {:answer/id #uuid "878bf775-d689-5f90-935e-bdbb9216b91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/ea348c364e2d05abb2adc5c86ce2d59e01ccc1c1d9e3e4ba7c189cc1cf3cb925.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571771} {:answer/id #uuid "8df859fc-145b-5e86-9c79-d402ed969101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/35/359aed8184fd2ae25a5290a013e68fb8068176286e8684cd13459df4e77e9693.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34d29957-a4c2-51f3-8772-9c52f4ca375c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c3/c371c84dedc8f76fe286a7f4201416c2c344d4718bdf61a80bd5c3da7a048cd4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571626} :answer-field/id #uuid "5428c292-72be-5b0f-bf8c-5686e732abae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99744ab1-80a8-57ad-804e-15c6f48c9bd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-119064" :question/problem "![](images/60/605c5def8bc643f0f601f89b9f8d7b556ac94206867dbe8904ef746c83f02fc0.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vector $a.$ Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $\\frac{3}{2}a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $\\frac{3}{2}a$ must be parallel to $a.$\nNow, we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $\\frac{3}{2}a$ is $\\frac{3}{2}$ of the magnitude of $a.$\n\n- Vectors $a$ and $\\frac{3}{2}a$ have the same direction since the factor $\\frac{3}{2}$ is positive.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is the following.\n\n![](images/59/591682cfbe0f50347d88f894f4c2b740fca140e8a93838f5c53022f9f50ee6da.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096648 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "27d5c96d-ca13-5c1e-83d3-0dc9f6da0f83" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Vectors are Parallel"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b9401b-8227-5b31-a1af-489974f90cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571693} {:answer/id #uuid "78af9df5-9c07-5149-afa4-47ce7f15a0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $\\lambda$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571747} {:answer/id #uuid "89eb437f-1651-5f56-bd87-3dcb712156b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571775} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d91dc1-da76-5e69-bffc-16bb4177a79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571823} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f5c7ac-9844-58a6-b692-649d36bbf0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5f5c7ac-9844-58a6-b692-649d36bbf0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571947} :answer-field/id #uuid "14754df4-59b3-5598-a9e7-143bba8252f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4c754c3-d143-5941-8c38-1a8c75e6be25" :question/math-academy-id "q-20395" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda (12a-52b)$ and $-3a+13b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n-3a+13b=\\lambda (12a-52b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{4}(12a-52b)=\\lambda (12a-52b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(12a-52b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=12a-52b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{4}u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096648 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "27d5c96d-ca13-5c1e-83d3-0dc9f6da0f83" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Vectors are Parallel"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3406a2e-3e30-5a10-afce-d9b951b31dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3406a2e-3e30-5a10-afce-d9b951b31dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571887} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d6a9ee6-1f19-56a5-9ce3-6b062583c4af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9cb3a4aa-4089-5a0f-987c-888c6fdaeaf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-324233" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda (4a+\\sqrt{7}b)$ and $4\\sqrt{7}\\,a+7b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n4\\sqrt{7}\\,a+7b=\\lambda (4a+\\sqrt{7}b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{7}(4a+\\sqrt{7}b)=\\lambda (4a+\\sqrt{7}b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(4a+\\sqrt{7}b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=4a+\\sqrt{7}b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{7}\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =\\sqrt{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc5bab6c-1ce7-58b5-a59d-cff2ce35ecca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3065f6cb-298c-5d20-ac8b-5527933c3f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571619} {:answer/id #uuid "37dc1911-7472-5dfc-be1b-13cdc7f8643f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571638} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1cd6d9-46ec-5f1d-b69f-f2f5151ce530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571696} {:answer/id #uuid "8cde6ed8-d2a2-51a5-85d9-0411a1bb9b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571781} {:answer/id #uuid "fddcd25a-ebf4-560d-b1af-2a98ce2e244e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3065f6cb-298c-5d20-ac8b-5527933c3f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571619} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b587d3b-55bf-5b89-b2c4-ae91f0538308" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571988}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "52f19af3-7870-568c-aad1-0f002a1758f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-69951" :question/problem "![](images/31/314cd1d2e150c078fa7232c81125de44fb8c26c176d2a1f32ab02fbae2eef299.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $m=-g$\n\nII. $a=z$\n\nIII. $g=-\\frac{1}{2}m$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The magnitude of $m$ is greater than the magnitude of $g.$ So, $m\\ne -g.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $a$ and $z$ have opposite directions. So, $a\\ne z.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, vectors $g$ and $m$ are parallel and have opposite directions. Also the magnitude of $g$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $m.$ So, $g=-\\frac{1}{2}m.$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572153 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc49f831-8e1d-5fb4-8952-1dd4ee3bfa02" :knowledge-point/title "Creating Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4834da0c-e138-5195-b5c7-e0793083032e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/2938ca5550faa3fb4c04daae1dc63a6dc86698a90a247fccd38fc034f5a7ff11.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571668} {:answer/id #uuid "70bf1955-e060-5bfb-849a-9bf126ad2269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/ae0235d72386ef97519d913dc5cef3da4699a92a18d5c037153020d75c21a3c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571731} {:answer/id #uuid "9f2a1653-575b-52cd-a682-b2b19dca8b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1dc14e69e650dd9081cbfb3769e21d49aa905b6d8b3a84d9dfaf935ba57a107e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571815} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e27537-9585-5713-8d2f-71f44be2c767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b2/b20f3879b4b9bd98aacd5bce58a1bc6241a2671e74ffb27374545acbe3975098.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571827} {:answer/id #uuid "ea4df393-61ca-5a1e-b8ec-00b075b26d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5d/5df7bba8e49cecb0ce082a7e8093478c032c90eae1ebccd5b3b3efed825b6f63.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea4df393-61ca-5a1e-b8ec-00b075b26d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5d/5df7bba8e49cecb0ce082a7e8093478c032c90eae1ebccd5b3b3efed825b6f63.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571952} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c52a915-0f05-5bb2-9874-890dcfeb7473" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9199d3db-0aa2-51c3-b858-22576fdfaa53" :question/math-academy-id "q-69960" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b2c3f59df41cb406ddfc41eea81a979dec578ba990032f0ff4f2f9792f58c8b2.png)\n\nThe vector $a$ is depicted above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vectors $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ and $2a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ and $2a$ must be parallel to $a.$\n\nNow, for the vector $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ is $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the magnitude of $a.$\n\n- Vectors $a$ and $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ have opposite directions since the factor $-\\frac{3}{4}$ is negative.\n\n![](images/13/13e4de227344b9eb7d1867cca0d05d9bcb647662a0c732398b42277ac379d361.png)\n\n \n\nNext, for the vector $2a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $2a$ is twice the magnitude of $a.$\n\n- Vectors $a$ and $2a$ have the same direction since the factor $2$ is positive.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is the following.\n\n![](images/13/13ca18bebfdb3c738d0a1198d0ce4235bfd77185bcf232f79f9ba089ce3b6d38.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc5bab6c-1ce7-58b5-a59d-cff2ce35ecca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b86a3d8-bbdc-510c-bdb1-25822dde58a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571647} {:answer/id #uuid "b55d5c71-dfbf-5d5c-b477-04b04d7dda95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571856} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ff3248-4b13-5d5b-9c41-dfbe5793add0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571900} {:answer/id #uuid "cdea4944-bf33-5ba6-9d6a-697b65a617dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571909} {:answer/id #uuid "d66f4a36-7bf8-5c75-8d2c-1dec7887829a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdea4944-bf33-5ba6-9d6a-697b65a617dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571909} :answer-field/id #uuid "471634b7-feb0-50b9-9eda-91e81c3b2ea0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f081ecc9-be21-500f-81d8-5fe5809e98ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-76939" :question/problem "![](images/92/9236e136f26433023d806181fcfbef9c05d4976f75e14f74840ae7f48a35da99.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $r=3q$\n\nII. $s=2t$\n\nIII. $p=-s$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $r$ and $q$ have the opposite directions. So, $r\\ne 3q.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $s$ and $t$ are parallel and have the same directions. Also, the magnitude of $s$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $t.$ So, $s=2t.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $p$ and $s$ are parallel and have the opposite directions. Also, their magnitudes are the same. So, $p=-s.$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, and statement I is false."}]}
